s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adp-sandbox-builder-ishan%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adp-sandbox-builder-ishan%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Spec for epic #1, revision 1. Lock = @dharishan04 approves the latest push.\n\n## Agent summary\nI wrote `specs/1.md` (revision 1) and `app/cases/1/history.spec.ts`. The spec still has one `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]`, so Lock will be refused until the lead answers it.\n\n**Requirements**\n- **FR-001:** `GET /sensors/{id}/history?from&to` returns 200 with `{ sensorId, readings: [{ at, value }] }`, containing only that sensor's readings in the range, oldest first.\n- **FR-002:** Both bounds are inclusive.\n- **FR-003:** An unknown sensor returns 404 with `{ \"error\": \"unknown_sensor\" }`.\n- **FR-004:** A range over the maximum returns 400 with `{ \"error\": \"range_too_large\" }`.\n- **SC-001:** One day of an hourly sensor returns exactly 25 readings in ascending order.\n- Milestone #2 covers all of these.\n\n**Cases:** each of the five tests in `history.spec.ts` covers one item.\n- Readings in range, oldest first, bounds inclusive: FR-001 and FR-002.\n- Readings outside the range excluded: FR-001.\n- A full day of hourly readings gives 25 in ascending order: SC-001.\n- Unknown sensor: FR-003. It asserts the exact error body, so the app's generic `not_found` 404 can't satisfy it.\n- Range over the limit: FR-004.\n\n**Decisions I made:**\n- I chose the response shape, the error code `range_too_large` and the inclusive bounds myself. They are noted under Clarifications.\n- I didn't change `openapi.yaml`, because the lead's note didn't ask for it.\n- Malformed or missing `from`/`to`, and `from` after `to`, are out of scope.\n\n**Tests:** I ran `npx playwright test cases/1`. All 5 tests fail because the history route doesn't exist yet: they get the generic 404 `not_found` instead of the expected response. None fail on syntax errors.\n\n**Open questions:**\n- What is the maximum allowed range for /history (for example 7 or 31 days)? This is the one NEEDS CLARIFICATION in FR-004. The cases hold for any limit between 1 day and about 4 years.\n\n### Provenance (written by the workflow)\n| agent role | model | plugin | where the agent ran | published by run | started by |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| builder | claude-sonnet-5-5 | delivery@0.1.0 | laptop (self-declared) | [39390066610](https://github.com/dharishan04/adp-sandbox/actions/runs/39390066610) | @dharishan04 |\n<!-- adp-provenance {\"role\":\"builder\",\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5-5\",\"plugin\":\"delivery@0.1.0\",\"run\":\"39390066610\",\"actor\":\"dharishan04\",\"sdk\":\"0.3.304\",\"where\":\"laptop\",\"session\":\"fff3c93e-4f72-49fb-83be-ad48ea45921d\"} -->\n\n---\n## Agent summary\nI amended `specs/1.md` (still revision 1) and `app/cases/1/history.spec.ts` for the lead's round-1 answers, and added the endpoint to `app/openapi.yaml`.\n\nRequirements:\n- **FR-001:** `GET /sensors/{id}/history?from&to` returns `{sensorId, readings[{at, value}]}`, only that sensor's readings, oldest first.\n- **FR-002:** both bounds are inclusive.\n- **FR-003:** an unknown sensor gets 404 `{error:\"unknown_sensor\"}`.\n- **FR-004:** a range over 7 days gets 400 `range_too_large`, and exactly 7 days is accepted. The `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` marker is gone, and the 7-day limit is recorded under Clarifications dated 2026-10-20.\n- **FR-005 (new):** an in-range window with no readings returns 200 with an empty array.\n- **FR-006 (new):** the endpoint is documented in `app/openapi.yaml`, with the response schema and the 400 and 404 errors (new `History` schema).\n- **SC-001:** a full day of hourly readings gives 25 readings in ascending order.\n\nClarifications also say that error precedence and timestamp formats are out of scope, along with missing/malformed bounds and `from` after `to`.\n\nCases (all in `app/cases/1/history.spec.ts`; the spec's `cases` and `milestones` front matter now cover FR-001 to FR-006 and SC-001):\n- **FR-001, FR-002:** the original range case (inclusive bounds, oldest first) and the \"excludes readings outside the range\" case.\n- **SC-001:** the full-day case.\n- **FR-001 (new):** only the requested sensor's readings. s-1 and s-2 get the same timestamps and different values.\n- **FR-005 (new):** a window with no readings returns `{sensorId, readings: []}`.\n- **FR-004 (new):** exactly 7 days is accepted (169 readings), and 7 days plus 1 second gets 400 `range_too_large`.\n- **FR-003:** an unknown sensor gets 404 with the exact body.\n- **FR-004:** the existing over-the-limit case, a 4-year range.\n- **FR-006:** no Playwright case. It is a documentation requirement.\n\nOne command was blocked by the delivery guard, which said `app/cases/1` is a locked case file. It had only mentioned that path in a read-only `ls`. I reran the inspection without it, and the later `Edit` to the case file went through. If the guard should have stopped that edit, the case-file change needs a second look.\n\n**Tests:** `cd app && npx playwright test cases/1`: 9 of 9 fail today. The cases get a 404 `not_found` from the missing route, so the status or exact-body assertions fail. Nothing fails on a syntax error.\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Was the guard's \"locked case file\" block a false positive on the read-only `ls`? The later edit to `app/cases/1/history.spec.ts` was allowed, which suggests it was.\n- FR-006 has no Playwright case, since it is a documentation requirement. It is attached to milestone #2 for coverage. Say if you want a different check for it.\n\n### Provenance (written by the workflow)\n| agent role | model | plugin | where the agent ran | published by run | started by |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| builder | claude-sonnet-5-5 | delivery@0.1.0 | laptop (self-declared) | [39390655667](https://github.com/dharishan04/adp-sandbox/actions/runs/39390655667) | @dharishan04 |\n<!-- adp-provenan